==================================================
PART 0-B — GIT, DATA AND IMPLEMENTATION SAFETY
==================================================

Continue the previous non-negotiable rules:

- Do not commit, push, merge or deploy without explicit approval.
- Do not overwrite .env files.
- Never print secrets in logs or reports.
- Never expose DATABASE_URL, database passwords, service-role keys or provider secrets in frontend bundles.
- Never assume a migration succeeded because its SQL file exists.
- Never assume cloud sync works because API endpoints exist.
- Never claim an integration is live without a real integration test.
- Never replace actual functionality with mock data to satisfy a test.
- Mocks are permitted only in isolated tests and clearly identified demos.
- No fake AI agents, fake embeddings, fake payments, fake cloud storage or fake integrations.
- Keep dependency additions justified, lightweight and compatible with the existing package manager.
- Do not install several libraries performing the same function.
- Preserve all existing user records and offline capabilities.
- Maintain backward compatibility wherever practical.
- Every new module must include loading, empty, error, success and permission-denied states.

If implementation exceeds available context:
1. Complete the current safe task.
2. Save a checkpoint.
3. Update the implementation matrix.
4. Record exact files changed and tests run.
5. Resume from the first incomplete task.
6. Never report incomplete work as complete.

