PART 10 — TESTING AND ACCEPTANCE RULES
==================================================

For every phase:

- Add tests with the feature.
- Run targeted tests.
- Run regression tests.
- Inspect failures.
- Fix root causes.
- Re-run affected tests.
- Document results.

Required database test scenarios:

A. Existing data remains intact.
B. Migration can run on an empty database.
C. Migration can safely handle an already migrated database.
D. Migration failure rolls back safely.
E. Workspace A cannot access Workspace B.
F. User A cannot access User B's private records.
G. Client cannot access internal notes.
H. Offline changes survive browser restart.
I. Duplicate sync requests do not duplicate records.
J. Conflict resolution does not silently lose financial data.
K. Revoked access immediately prevents protected operations.
L. Deleted cloud records propagate correctly through tombstones.

AI test scenarios:

A. Read-only agents cannot write.
B. Draft-only agents cannot send.
C. Approval-required agents cannot bypass approval.
D. Orchestrator cannot expand child permissions.
E. Prompt injection cannot change permission scope.
F. Restricted knowledge is not retrieved.
G. Unsupported answers are marked uncertain.
H. Citations point to retrieved source records.
I. Cancellation works.
J. Usage and cost limits work.

Finance tests:

- Decimal arithmetic.
- Rounding.
- Tax.
- Discounts.
- Refunds.
- Partial payments.
- Duplicate payments.
- Currency conversions.
- Negative values.
- Very large values.
- Timezone boundaries.

